@startuml
title Command Product Lifecycle (simulation)
actor Operator
participant "Mission Control" as MCS
participant "Command Validator" as Validator
participant "Pass Scheduler" as Scheduler
participant "DSN Uplink Processor" as Uplink
participant "Delayed Link" as Link
participant "CCS Model" as CCS
participant "Event/Audit Store" as Audit
Operator -> MCS : create command product
MCS -> Validator : validate product
Validator --> MCS : validation report
MCS -> Audit : record draft/validation
MCS -> Scheduler : request contact slot
Scheduler --> MCS : scheduled / queued
MCS -> Uplink : release approved product
Uplink -> Audit : record transmission start
Uplink -> Link : transmit command
Link -> CCS : deliver after simulated light-time
CCS --> Link : receipt / rejection event
Link --> Uplink : delayed acknowledgement event
Uplink -> Audit : record receipt evidence
note over CCS,Audit
Transmission does not prove execution.
Execution and later telemetry evidence are separate events.
end note
@enduml
